      "hideComponent": "false",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><i>4-minute read</i></span></p>\n<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\">Where to place AED pads on adults and children</span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">In the critical moments of a sudden cardiac arrest, the proper use of an automated external defibrillator (AED) can help determine the outcome of the event. When the heart unexpectedly falls into a shockable rhythm, an AED becomes an invaluable tool to provide an opportunity to restore an organized rhythm. However, the effectiveness of this life-saving device is heavily contingent upon the correct placement of its pads on the patient’s body.<sup>1</sup> </span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The pads must be positioned correctly precisely to help ensure the electrical current passes through the heart muscle effectively. Clear visual cues and instructions as well as voice prompts typically accompany an AED, guiding even an untrained bystander through the process.</span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 19:29:28 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "bottomMargin": "5"
    },
    "cols2": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:03:40 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:03:40 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 16:29:01 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\">Anterior-lateral placement of AED pads</span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">When employing the anterior-lateral placement, one pad should be positioned on the right side of the patient's chest, specifically beneath the clavicle, or collarbone.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The corresponding pad is then placed on the left side of the patient’s chest. It is situated below the level of the pectoral muscles, carefully avoiding the breast tissue.</span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 19:29:06 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "katie.boertman@stryker.com",
          "preset": "max_width_1440",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 16:29:26 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "Anterior-lateral placement of AED pads",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/ems/news/images/aed-pad-placement_adult-anterior-lateral-front.jpg",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 30 2024 12:35:05 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      }
    },
    "cols2_copy": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:03:40 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:03:40 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 16:29:01 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\">Anterior-posterior placement of AED pads</span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">While the standard positioning of AED pads is typically lateral, with one pad placed to the right of the sternum and the other below the left breast, there are certain clinical scenarios where an anterior-posterior configuration is advantageous. This alternative method involves positioning one pad on the chest (anterior), while the corresponding pad is adhered to the back (posterior), directly behind the first pad.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This placement is also helpful when a patient has a medical implant such as a pacemaker or implantable cardioverter-defibrillator, which might be damaged by electrical shock or divert energy from the heart.</span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:38:55 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "preset": "max_width_1440",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 16:29:26 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "Anterior-posterior placement of AED pads",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/ems/news/images/aed-pad-placement_adult-anterior-posterior-female.jpg",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Oct 24 2024 15:24:49 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
