        }
      }
    },
    "cols2_copy_1045413852": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:03:40 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:03:40 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 16:29:01 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\">Pad placement on children</span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">When it comes to AED pad placement on adults, the anterior-lateral position is the standard. However, for children under the age of 8 or weighing less than 55 pounds (25 kilograms), special considerations are needed.<br>\n</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">If available, use pediatric pads and an AED with a pediatric dose attenuator.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">For young children with small chests, use the anterior-posterior pad placement method. Place one pad in the center of the chest and the other on the back between the shoulder blades. Using pads with the anterior-posterior placement method ensures that the pads do not overlap or touch each other.</span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:39:06 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "preset": "max_width_1440",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 16:29:26 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "Pad placement on children",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/ems/news/images/aed-pad-placement_pediatric-anterior-posterior-child.jpg",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Oct 24 2024 15:26:43 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      }
    },
    "text": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Mon Sep 23 2024 17:10:53 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\">The Importance of correct AED pad placement</span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Correct pad placement is needed for several reasons:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Maximizes the effectiveness of the shock delivered to the heart.</b> Proper placement of the pads helps ensure the electrical current follows the most direct path through the heart. This helps maximize the chance of restoring a normal heart rhythm.<sup>2<br>\n <br>\n</sup> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Reduces the risk of burns under the pads.</b> Correct pad placement on dry skin can help minimize the risk of skin burns. Moisture can reduce the adhesion of pads to the chest wall and negatively affect the effectiveness of the AED shocks, potentially causing burns when the shock is delivered.<sup>3<br>\n <br>\n </sup></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Protects the safety of the rescuer and bystanders.</b> By following the recommended pad placement guidelines, rescuers reduce the risk of an accidental shock to themselves or bystanders.<sup>4</sup></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><b data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Together, we save lives.</span></b></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The correct placement of AED pads is a critical component of effective defibrillation. Whether it's the anterior-lateral or anterior-posterior method, understanding the proper techniques for both adults and children can increase the chances of survival in sudden cardiac emergencies.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">AEDs are designed with simplicity in mind to empower anyone to be a lifesaver. Stryker’s line of AEDs offers several options to best suit your needs. With more than a million AEDs deployed globally, Stryker offers diverse options and deep expertise to help you choose the right device and cost-effectively manage your AED program.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><a href=\"https://www.stryker.com/us/en/emergency-care/community-public-safety.html\">Connect with an AED expert</a> to learn more about our AEDs and how we can help make your community safer.&nbsp;</span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 23 2024 18:02:20 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
